---
const base = "/studies/drone-launcher-2026-11-25";
---

<figure>
  <div class="specimen">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 40 27"
      role="img"
      aria-label="Launcher and drone masters at the same drawing scale, preserving their source proportions"
    >
      <title>Launcher and drone · same drawing scale</title>
      <image
        href={`${base}/02-1-launcher-master.svg`}
        x="7"
        y="1.5"
        width="8.505661"
        height="22.138202"
      />
      <image
        href={`${base}/02-1-drone-master.svg`}
        x="24"
        y="3.737112"
        width="5.428502"
        height="9.39426"
      />
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Same drawing scale for both objects. The drone is approximately 42.4% of the
    launcher's length, including its original blue exhaust. Black background
    matches the draft. This is an enlarged form inspection; world size is
    unassigned.
  </figcaption>
  <div class="downloads">
    <a href={`${base}/02-1-launcher-master.svg`}>Launcher SVG master</a>
    <a href={`${base}/02-1-drone-master.svg`}>Drone SVG master</a>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
figure {
  margin: var(--spacing-xl) 0;
}
.specimen {
  background: #000;
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
}
svg {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
figcaption {
  max-width: var(--measure-prose);
  margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}
.downloads {
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
}
a:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-selected);
  outline-offset: 4px;
}
</style>
